{
  "question": "What is the cause of the statistically significant lagged correlation (≈5‑day offset) between pendulum_lab and resonator_obs readings, given the modest upward drift observed in resonator_obs (z = 2.10) and the overall absence of systematic drift or level changes in the other instruments?",
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "label": "H1: Random coincidence",
      "probability": 0.15,
      "rationale": "All cross‑instrument agreements are modest and most fall within their calculated chance thresholds. The apparent 5‑day correlation could be a statistical fluctuation arising from the many lag tests performed.",
      "evidenceFor": ["cross_corr_5d"],
      "evidenceAgainst": ["drift_resonator_obs_z2.10", "drift_pendulum_lab_z-0.06", "drift_pendulum_obs_z0.64", "drift_resonator_lab_z-0.43"]
    },
    {
      "label": "H2: Delayed shared environmental influence",
      "probability": 0.30,
      "rationale": "A slow‑varying factor (e.g., temperature, humidity, power line fluctuations) could affect the resonator_obs apparatus with a delay of several days, producing a lagged correlation with the nearby pendulum_lab which reacts more promptly. The resonator_obs upward drift (z = 2.10) supports an external influence that is not present in the other instruments.",
      "evidenceFor": ["cross_corr_5d", "drift_resonator_obs_z2.10"],
      "evidenceAgainst": ["lack_of_drift_pendulum_lab", "lack_of_drift_pendulum_obs", "lack_of_drift_resonator_lab"]
    },
    {
      "label": "H3: Systematic timing / data‑logging artefact",
      "probability": 0.30,
      "rationale": "Pendulum_lab and resonator_obs data are streamed through the same central logging server. A recurring offset in how batches are timestamped or written could generate an apparent correlation at a specific lag without altering the underlying physical measurements. This would explain why only the pendulum_lab–resonator_obs pair shows significance while other pairings do not.",
      "evidenceFor": ["cross_corr_5d", "identical_timestamp_source"],
      "evidenceAgainst": ["stable_baseline_behaviour_in_all_instruments", "no_known_change_in_logging_software"]
    },
    {
      "label": "H4: External data‑generation or manipulation",
      "probability": 0.10,
      "rationale": "An outside process (e.g., automated script, remote tampering) could be inserting or altering values specifically for pendulum_lab and resonator_obs, producing a patterned lagged relationship. The modest drift in resonator_obs and the isolated 5‑day correlation are compatible with a deliberately crafted data stream designed to mimic natural variability.",
      "evidenceFor": ["cross_corr_5d", "drift_resonator_obs_z2.10"],
      "evidenceAgainst": ["no_direct evidence_of_access_or_modification", "consistent instrument performance elsewhere"]
    }
  ],
  "residual": 0.15,
  "summaryOfChange": "The question was refined to focus on the specific 5‑day lagged correlation between pendulum_lab and resonator_obs, incorporating the newly observed resonator_obs upward drift (z = 2.10). Probabilities were updated: the random‑coincidence hypothesis was reduced (from 0.25 to 0.15) because the correlation exceeds its chance threshold; the environmental‑coupling and timing‑artefact hypotheses were each raised to 0.30 in light of the drift evidence and the plausibility of a shared logging pipeline; the external‑data hypothesis retained a low but non‑negligible weight (0.10); and a residual 0.15 was allocated for any unconsidered mechanism. All changes are explicitly justified by the latest baseline and drift statistics and by the presence of the 5‑day lagged correlation."
}

